WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 008, en. Timings estimated from the script until the clip is rendered (re-split 27 Oct 2026: <=2x42 chars, <=20 cps, <=180 wpm).

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.807
<v Nia>When does Tŷ Mawr first appear by name?

2
00:00:02.927 --> 00:00:05.860
<v Nia>In the papers we hold,
eighteen twenty- four.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.789
<v the Bute estate agent>Bore da, Miss Nia. Mind
the ink, it's still drying.

4
00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:14.976
<v the Bute estate agent>This is Mr David Stewart's survey of
the Bute estates, eighteen twenty-four.

5
00:00:15.096 --> 00:00:16.396
<v the Bute estate agent>Plan nineteen.

6
00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.570
<v Nia>Cedfin or Ty Mawr Farm.

7
00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.497
<v Nia>Two names for one farm, side by side.

8
00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:26.751
<v Nia>Today the Glamorgan Archives catalogue
files it as Cedfin alias Ty Mawr farm,

9
00:00:26.871 --> 00:00:28.171
<v Nia>in Llandough.

10
00:00:28.591 --> 00:00:32.724
<v the Bute estate agent>One hundred and thirty-nine acres,
three roods, eight perches.

11
00:00:32.844 --> 00:00:37.444
<v the Bute estate agent>Of that, twenty acres, two roods
and thirty-five perches is woodland.

12
00:00:37.864 --> 00:00:41.373
<v Nia>And the occupier? I read
that hand as John Gedrick,

13
00:00:41.493 --> 00:00:45.352
<v Nia>but I'd want a second pair
of eyes on those letters.

14
00:00:45.772 --> 00:00:47.172
<v the Bute estate agent>Gedrick, near enough.

15
00:00:47.292 --> 00:00:52.559
<v the Bute estate agent>And mark this corner: ten acres, three
roods, thirty-nine perches of late Thos.

16
00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:54.279
<v the Bute estate agent>Williams land, added in.

17
00:00:54.699 --> 00:00:58.032
<v Nia>A Williams on this ground
in eighteen twenty-four.

18
00:00:58.152 --> 00:01:01.310
<v Nia>The plan shows his land joined to Ty Mawr.

19
00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:05.290
<v Nia>It doesn't show who he was,
or how it came across.

20
00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:10.976
<v Nia>The family wiki holds an uploaded picture
titled eighteen twenty-four map of Ty

21
00:01:11.096 --> 00:01:15.307
<v Nia>Mawr. Nobody has pinned down who
drew it, its scale, its sheet,

22
00:01:15.427 --> 00:01:17.094
<v Nia>where the original lives,

23
00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.147
<v Nia>or whether eighteen twenty-four
is even the map's own date.

24
00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:26.167
<v the Bute estate agent>Then lay it beside plan nineteen,
madam, and let the lines settle it.

25
00:01:26.587 --> 00:01:29.720
<v Nia>Exactly. Until they're
matched, it's a picture,

26
00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.707
<v Nia>not proof of any boundary
registered later.

27
00:01:33.127 --> 00:01:37.660
<v Nia>Then this one, saved in the media
library as eighteen forty-one map.

28
00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.640
<v Nia>No title we can trust,
no survey date, no archive number.

29
00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.260
<v the Bute estate agent>Seventeen years after Mr Stewart?

30
00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:47.889
<v the Bute estate agent>Then the tithe men will
have been busy in Llandough.

31
00:01:48.309 --> 00:01:52.842
<v Nia>They were. The eighteen forty-one
tithe apportionment for Llandough,

32
00:01:52.962 --> 00:01:56.095
<v Nia>Cogan and Leckwith survives
as the parish copy,

33
00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:59.149
<v Nia>Glamorgan Archives P
thirty-five stroke ten.

34
00:01:59.569 --> 00:02:03.169
<v Nia>But nothing yet ties this
image to that apportionment,

35
00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:07.755
<v Nia>and neither picture proves ownership,
possession or any conveyance.

36
00:02:08.175 --> 00:02:11.375
<v the Bute estate agent>Then you'll be wanting
the apportionment itself.

37
00:02:11.795 --> 00:02:13.195
<v Nia>First thing tomorrow.

38
00:02:13.315 --> 00:02:18.582
<v Nia>Let's follow those Williamses forward
and see when Great House farm turns up in

39
00:02:18.702 --> 00:02:20.002
<v Nia>print.
